WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:09.218
Ben sighed with relief as the owl flew over to Waldo.

2
00:00:09.219 --> 00:00:15.882
"Drop!" Waldo said, and Oswald released the kitten.

3
00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:18.719
Winnie ran over to scoop up Inky.

4
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.414
Then she looked up and glared at Waldo.

5
00:00:21.415 --> 00:00:24.285
"Oswald could have eaten her, Waldo!"

6
00:00:24.286 --> 00:00:27.566
Waldo hung his head. "I'm really sorry, Winnie.

7
00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:29.325
Oswald has a mind of his own.

8
00:00:29.326 --> 00:00:34.105
And it's hard to train a pet who's invisible half the time."

9
00:00:34.106 --> 00:00:36.623
"That's for sure!" Ben chimed in.

10
00:00:36.624 --> 00:00:43.033
Winnie cuddled her kitten for a few minutes and then let out a breath.

11
00:00:43.034 --> 00:00:47.030
"Inky seems fine. Thanks for saving the day, Ben.

12
00:00:47.031 --> 00:00:52.053
I had no idea what was going on when she shot up in the air like that."

13
00:00:52.054 --> 00:00:58.033
Ben nodded. "Sid's spots were the clue. I realized Oswald was nearby."

14
00:00:58.034 --> 00:01:02.031
"I guess I'm allergic to owls too," Sid mumbled.

15
00:01:02.032 --> 00:01:05.386
"Have you thought about a pet rock?" Waldo joked.

16
00:01:05.387 --> 00:01:10.865
Ben rolled his eyes. "Not funny," he said.

17
00:01:10.866 --> 00:01:16.074
*** Once things had calmed down, the pet tricks show

18
00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.920
continued. Ben was rooting for Winnie or Mog to

19
00:01:18.921 --> 00:01:25.047
win. But he enjoyed watching other pets do tricks, especially Pixel's pig and two

20
00:01:25.048 --> 00:01:29.524
dogs. A ghoul hound spun a ball on its nose, like a seal.

21
00:01:29.525 --> 00:01:34.741
A skeleton dog impressed everyone by fetching bones.

22
00:01:34.742 --> 00:01:40.766
After all the pets had performed, the judges huddled on the stage.

23
00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:46.306
Finally they signaled to Miss Bungle that they had selected a winner.

24
00:01:46.307 --> 00:01:49.961
She smiled as she stood in front of the microphone.

25
00:01:49.962 --> 00:01:56.661
"And the first-place winner is . . . Priscilla, the pet pig!

26
00:01:56.662 --> 00:02:04.986
Second place goes to Slimy, the singing slug."

27
00:02:04.987 --> 00:02:08.795
"Yes!" Waldo cried. "Jen won a prize!"

28
00:02:08.796 --> 00:02:17.067
"So did Pixel," Ben said.

29
00:02:17.068 --> 00:02:22.737
"Our next event will be the obedience show," Miss Bungle announced.

30
00:02:22.738 --> 00:02:25.772
"It will start in about one hour.

31
00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:32.450
And after that comes our final event of the weekend—the best pet competition.

32
00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:37.866
While you're waiting for the next show, please visit our pet adoption booth.

33
00:02:37.867 --> 00:02:43.458
We have some wonderful pets there who need great homes."

34
00:02:43.459 --> 00:02:46.057
Ben and Sid looked at each other.

35
00:02:46.058 --> 00:02:49.485
"I have more volunteer duties right now," Ben said.

36
00:02:49.486 --> 00:02:59.841
"But we can try to check it out later."

37
00:02:59.842 --> 00:03:04.354
*** Ben and Sid found a couple of good seats for the obedience

38
00:03:04.355 --> 00:03:12.322
contest. Mrs. Hubbletree hurried onstage first, beaming as she held up her valuable rainbow gecko for everyone to

39
00:03:12.323 --> 00:03:15.311
see. Ben noticed that she had gotten dressed up for the

40
00:03:15.312 --> 00:03:18.902
event. She had on a colorful dress with a matching

41
00:03:18.903 --> 00:03:23.599
handbag. "Rainbow geckos are very rare," the mayor's wife said

42
00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:26.223
proudly. "Especially in People

43
00:03:26.224 --> 00:03:33.323
Place. Bowie can change to any color—sometimes he even changes to

44
00:03:33.324 --> 00:03:36.962
patterns." "Can we see?" a monster shouted from the front

45
00:03:36.963 --> 00:03:40.123
row. "Sure!" Mrs. Hubbletree said

46
00:03:40.124 --> 00:03:42.993
proudly. "I'll

47
00:03:42.994 --> 00:03:47.106
demonstrate." She spread several colorful fabric squares on a

48
00:03:47.107 --> 00:03:53.551
table. Each time Bowie was placed on a fabric square, he matched the color and pattern

49
00:03:53.552 --> 00:03:58.195
perfectly. "That is pretty amazing," Ben said and others

50
00:03:58.196 --> 00:04:04.427
nodded. A judge smiled politely. "Lizard behavior is quite fascinating, Mrs.

51
00:04:04.428 --> 00:04:09.020
Hubbletree. But I'm afraid it's not really a demonstration of a pet's

52
00:04:09.021 --> 00:04:14.790
obedience." "Oh." Mrs. Hubbletree hung her head, looking deflated. "Are you

53
00:04:14.791 --> 00:04:17.093
sure?" The three judges

54
00:04:17.094 --> 00:04:22.182
nodded. She hurried offstage, and one by one, other pets

55
00:04:22.183 --> 00:04:27.500
performed. As he watched, Ben couldn't help thinking that none of them seemed very

56
00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:31.644
talented. A goblin fish just swam around its

57
00:04:31.645 --> 00:04:37.299
bowl. A spider scurried around the stage instead of following a "stay"

58
00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:44.049
command. Right now a skinny cat was supposed to be heeling, but all she did was stare off into space.

59
00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.362
The judges looked bored.

60
00:04:46.363 --> 00:04:51.010
"Next," one called, propping up his head in his hand.

61
00:04:51.011 --> 00:04:53.631
The show continued.

62
00:04:53.638 --> 00:04:56.095
At last it was Mog's turn.

63
00:04:56.096 --> 00:05:01.325
"Go, Mog!" Ben watched his friend take the stage with his two-headed dog.

64
00:05:01.326 --> 00:05:05.555
Everyone clapped as Rex-Rex perfectly followed Mog's commands.

65
00:05:05.556 --> 00:05:12.631
The dog sat, heeled, and lay down.

66
00:05:12.632 --> 00:05:15.238
"He's helpful too," Mog said.

67
00:05:15.239 --> 00:05:20.371
He demonstrated how Rex-Rex could open a latch, and find shoes.

68
00:05:20.372 --> 00:05:23.732
"He can retrieve both of my shoes at once!"

69
00:05:23.733 --> 00:05:27.929
The audience applauded as Mog and his dog finished performing.

70
00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:33.491
"Nice job," Ben thought. It had been a strong, solid performance.

71
00:05:33.492 --> 00:05:37.565
Suddenly the skinny cat's owner rushed toward the stage.

72
00:05:37.566 --> 00:05:39.650
"Excuse me!" she called.

73
00:05:39.651 --> 00:05:42.785
"Judges, please look at this! I got my cat to heel!"

74
00:05:42.786 --> 00:05:46.770
She ran onstage, her cat closely following her.

75
00:05:46.771 --> 00:05:50.541
A judge frowned. "Excuse me! You can't—"

76
00:05:50.542 --> 00:05:54.057
Hiss! The cat froze as she spotted Rex-Rex.

77
00:05:54.058 --> 00:05:59.739
Hissing again, she arched her back and stared at him.

78
00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:03.899
A low growl started in each Rex's throat.

79
00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:09.008
Then the two-headed dog barked like mad.

80
00:06:09.009 --> 00:06:13.918
The cat took off, and Rex-Rex chased after her!

